.TH HAILLO 1 "FEBRUARY 2025" Linux "User Manuals"
.SH NAME
Haillo \- a pseudo-terminal multiplexer for hai (hcli_hai), the HCLI command line AI chat and agent application.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B haillo
[ option | <command> ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B haillo
is a python pseudo-terminal multiplexer (pty mux) and terminal UI for hai (hcli_hai), the HCLI command line AI chat and agent application.
.sp
The pty mux can be invoked via python package name (simply typing haillo in the terminal after installing haillo via pip). The script is tied into python package version dependencies to help maintain semantic expectations, notably against huckle and hcli_hai.
.sp
Note that huckle must be setup to interact with the hcli_hai backend for haillo to be able to make use of hai (e.g. huckle cli install localhost:10000 (e.g. where hcli_hai could be running on hcli_core)).
.SH COMMANDS
.IP help
This help file.
.SH OPTIONS
.IP --version
.B haillo
version and the version of it's dependencies.
.SH EXAMPLE
haillo
.sp
haillo help
.sp
haillo --version
